  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sajid vs State Of U.P. And Another on 4 February, 2025 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ? Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:15714 Court No. - 77 Case :- Application U/S 528 Bnss No. - 3326 of 2025 Applicant :- Sajid Opposite Party :- State of U.P. and Another Counsel for Applicant :- Rajesh Pratap Singh Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Arun Kumar Singh Deshwal,J. 1. Heard Shri Rajesh Pratap Singh, learned counsel for the applicant and Shri Pankaj Saxena, learned Aga for the State. 2. The instant application has been filed by applicant for quashing the order dated 29.11.2024 passed by Additional District Magistrate (Administration)/Adjudicating Officer Azamgarh in Case No. 1672 of 2024 (State of Uttar Pradesh Vs. Sazid and others), under Section 51 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, P.S.- Nizamabad, District- Azamgarh.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "3. Learned A.G.A. has raised preliminary objection against the impugned order, there is a provision of appeal under Section 70 of Food Safety and Standards Act 2006. The applicant could not make out the case of exceptional nature, which could pursue this Court to entertain this application despite being having statutory remedy of appeal. 4. Learned counsel for the applicant submitted that he wants to withdraw the present application to avail the remedy to file an appeal under Section 70 of Food Safety and Standards Act 2006.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned A.G.A. has raised preliminary objection against the impugned order, there is a provision of appeal under Section 70 of Food Safety and Standards Act 2006. The applicant could not make out the case of exceptional nature, which could pursue this Court to entertain this application despite being having statutory remedy of appeal. 4. Learned counsel for the applicant submitted that he wants to withdraw the present application to avail the remedy to file an appeal under Section 70 of Food Safety and Standards Act 2006.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
